      "writtenOn": "2023-05-18T03:54:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For this specific issue, I think sending broadcast after `mNetworkActive \u003d activityParams.isActive` is enough.\n\nLinter complained about `handleReportNetworkActivity` since we have `@GuardedBy` annotation to `mNetworkActive` and `mActiveIdleTimers` \nBut after this CL,  only `isDefaultNetworkActive` and `dump` are called form non handler thread.\nThey only have read access to `mNetworkActive` and `mActiveIdleTimers`.\n\n`mNetworkActive` and `mActiveIdleTimers` are updated only from handler thread.\nSo, I don’t think we need lock in following cases.\n1. Read access to them from handler thread\n2. Update only `mNetworkActive` from handler thread \n\nIf above my thought is correct, I think we can go one of following direction\n1. Remove @GuardedBy annotation and acquire lock when needed.\n2. Keep @GuardedBy annotation and suppress lint when lock is not needed.\n3. Keep @GuardedBy annotation and ignore lint warning when lock is not needed.\n4. Keep @GuardedBy annotation and acquire lock at all access.\n\nI prefer 1 or 3 now but I want to ask feedback.",
      "parentUuid": "901200fa_77944c36",
